# Force LF line endings for shell scripts regardless of platform/git config on
# checkout - Windows Git commonly defaults to core.autocrlf=true, silently
# converting LF to CRLF on checkout. bash cannot parse CRLF-terminated lines
# correctly (each line's trailing \r becomes part of the last token/command,
# producing "$'\r': command not found" and similar corrupted-parsing errors) -
# this was hit directly when Jenkins' native Windows git checked out
# incluster-run.sh for the first time, despite the file working perfectly when
# checked out via WSL2's own Linux git throughout all manual testing.
*.sh text eol=lf
